{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ifelse_gathered_scalar_static",
  "description": "An observed with NO declared shape, `X = ifelse(lev < 2, F / D, 0.0)`, whose array arm divides a `cell`-shaped parameter by a scalar observed defined by a gather from an inline `const` table: `D = const[31, 28, 31][m]`, and (`D2`) the same table at interp.linear's cell index, a rank-0 `faq` count (the NEI2016 emission observeds as reseact builds them, `flux_CO / days_in_month …`). A gather with scalar subscripts is a scalar, so the build gives `X` the `cell` shape before it evaluates anything (esm-spec §4.3.4), and the scalar arm fills every element: condition true and false, the array arm first and second.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "native",
   "conformance"
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "cell": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 3
  }
 },
